exports[`lathe diff machine formats are locked > --format github (annotations + markdown, and the job summary) > stdout 1`] = `
"::error title=API breaking: operation-removed::deleteOrder — \`DELETE /orders/:id\` no longer exists (affects deleteOrder, useDeleteOrder (orders))
::notice title=API additive: field-added::Order.dueAt — string (optional) (affects getOrder, useGetOrder (orders))
### API contract: 1 breaking, 1 additive

#### Breaking (1)

Existing, correct client code can now be wrong at RUNTIME — it still typechecks against the regenerated types.

| Change | Subject | Detail | Generated code affected |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| \`operation-removed\` | \`deleteOrder\` | \`DELETE /orders/:id\` no longer exists | \`deleteOrder\`, \`useDeleteOrder\` (orders) |

#### Additive (1)

Nothing existing breaks; new surface is available.

| Change | Subject | Detail | Generated code affected |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| \`field-added\` | \`Order.dueAt\` | string (optional) | \`getOrder\`, \`useGetOrder\` (orders) |

<sub>Generated by <code>lathe diff</code> — severities are from the client’s point of view.</sub>

"
`;

